notes/secrets.env
*.env
*.env.local
*.env.*.local
.netlify/

# THE RUNNING SYSTEM WRITES THESE. Tracking a file the system rewrites makes
# the checkout permanently dirty and every `git pull` a conflict -- which is
# exactly what fks-services has been in: `.maintenance-baseline.json` is
# rewritten nightly by maintenance.py (new `ts`, new `disk_pct`), so `git
# status` there has shown ` M .maintenance-baseline.json` since August and a
# pull would have collided on it forever.
.maintenance-baseline.json

# db/ is STATE, all of it, not just server.db. This said `db/server.db` and
# nothing else, so control.db, fleet.json and changewatch.json all showed as
# untracked on both boxes -- and, worse, bank.db was one `git add .` away from
# being committed. kernel/bank.py holds secrets in that file and its own
# docstring says it is missed by backup rather than refused; it must be missed
# by git by RULE, not by nobody having typed the wrong command yet.
db/

# CLAUDE.md is your personal workspace config (real IPs, SSH user, etc.)
# Copy CLAUDE.example.md → CLAUDE.md and fill in your values.
# It is intentionally gitignored so credentials never reach GitHub.
CLAUDE.md

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.pyc
